[
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is my attempt:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨯</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">casesOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">λ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">i₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">casesOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">λ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And here is the error message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Application</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">argument</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨯</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span>\n<span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">application</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>How is the actual type not the same as the expected?  I'm stumped!</p>",
        "id": 626337755,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790173891
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When I put this into the web editor I get an error on <code>⨯</code>, <code>expected token</code>. Perhaps you meant <code>×</code> instead?</p>",
        "id": 626339272,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1790174171
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is <code>\\x</code> (<code>×</code>) vs <code>\\X</code> (<code>⨯</code>). The first one is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Prod#doc\">docs#Prod</a> (the one you probably want) but the second one is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Limits.prod#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Limits.prod</a>.</p>",
        "id": 626340010,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790174236
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, \\x and \\X are distinct, but indistinguishable to my eyes in the dark theme of Vscode.  A close look at the errors I pasted in a light mode show a slight difference.</p>",
        "id": 626342960,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790174662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Problem solved, and yes, now I also see that the two types need not be of the same universe.  Though they can't be of Sort 0, which I don't quite yet understand.</p>",
        "id": 626342981,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790174665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been bit by a similar error (with other symbols) in the past. Are there browsable lists of Mathlib symbols somewhere (preferably, with the associated VScode default shortcuts)? This would be a very useful feature to add to the documentation pages, IMHO (assuming there isn't one; if there is, then it would be a very useful link to add in a prominent place in the docs pages).</p>",
        "id": 626343110,
        "sender_full_name": "Philippe Duchon",
        "timestamp": 1790174687
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So as I got better accustomed to the notation, I found a shorter and more general proof.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 626345010,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790175042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can give you an even shorter \"proof\":</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TypeStar</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>... because this already exists as <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=instInhabitedProd#doc\">docs#instInhabitedProd</a></p>",
        "id": 626345686,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790175172
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And here's how this instance is written:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 626345950,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790175222
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873547\">Robin Arnez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Trying.20to.20prove.20.22product.20of.20inhabited.20types.20is.20inhabited.22/near/626345950\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And here's how this instance is written:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm learning from \"Theorem Proving in Lean\" and not yet at the chapter about type classes, but I have some notion of what they mean from Haskell, and analogous things in programming like Rust traits.</p>",
        "id": 626346756,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790175380
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another suggested exercise at this point is \"a function to an inhabited type is inhabited.\"</p>",
        "id": 626346938,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790175418
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Easily done</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">λ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 626347359,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790175504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And in the above, unlike with the product, α or β or both can be Sort 0</p>",
        "id": 626347883,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Licameli",
        "timestamp": 1790175605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"726077\">Philippe Duchon</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Trying.20to.20prove.20.22product.20of.20inhabited.20types.20is.20inhabited.22/near/626343110\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I've been bit by a similar error (with other symbols) in the past. Are there browsable lists of Mathlib symbols somewhere (preferably, with the associated VScode default shortcuts)? This would be a very useful feature to add to the documentation pages, IMHO (assuming there isn't one; if there is, then it would be a very useful link to add in a prominent place in the docs pages).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In VSCode, <code>ctrl/cmd + shift + P</code> -&gt; <code>Lean 4: Docs: Show Unicode Input Abbreviations</code>, and you can add a keybinding if you want</p>",
        "id": 626353096,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1790176590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! But this lets you find out how to type a symbol (or rather, what symbol a given abbreviation will produce), but not what it stands for in Mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 626468738,
        "sender_full_name": "Philippe Duchon",
        "timestamp": 1790204034
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you know what symbol you're looking for you can <code>#help term \"×\"</code> and control-click the results in the infoview to find out what it means.</p>\n<p>If you know what area you're interested in you can check out the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib-phrasebook/\">mathlib phrasebook</a> to see what the available concepts are and their notations.</p>\n<p>If you mean something unstructured like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_mathematical_symbols\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_mathematical_symbols</a> then I don't think there is one, but I'm also not sure when such a thing would be useful.</p>",
        "id": 626470038,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1790204353
    }
]